class:: TriggerDetector
summary:: Normalized envelope threshold and active-low diagnostic
categories:: UGens>Analysis
related:: Guides/MIRa-MS20-ESP

description::
Three binary outputs: trigger, gate, hardwareGate. Trigger lasts one control evaluation on activation. Gate is one while active; hardwareGate is its inverse (one inactive, zero active). No volts are emitted. There is no periodic retrigger option.

All parameters except the signal input are construction-time numbers. Outputs are control rate. See the guide for calibration, clipping, latency and model limitations.

classmethods::
method:: kr

argument:: envelope
Control-rate normalized envelope; audio-rate input is rejected.

argument:: threshold
Normalized activation threshold.

argument:: hysteresis
Normalized Schmitt half-width.

argument:: mode
Literal \digital or \circuit; both use the documented reduced Schmitt model.

returns::
Three binary outputs: trigger, gate, hardwareGate. Trigger lasts one control evaluation on activation. Gate is one while active; hardwareGate is its inverse (one inactive, zero active). No volts are emitted. There is no periodic retrigger option.

examples::
code::
{ TriggerDetector.kr(EnvFollow2.kr(SinOsc.ar(220, 0, 4))).poll; Silent.ar(2) }.play;
::
